  "texts": {
    "preamble": "G.Vijayakumar vs Designated Officer on 18 April, 2024 Crl.O.P.(MD) Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 18.04.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice A.A.Nakkiran Crl.O.P.(MD) No.23104 of 2022 and Crl.M.P.(MD).Nos.16391 & 16392 of 2022 G.Vijayakumar ... Petitioner / Accused Vs. Designated Officer, Code No.24-012, Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Madurai District. ... Respondent/Complainant Prayer: Criminal Original Petition is filed under Section 482 of Cr.P.C, to call for the records and quash the proceedings in S.T.C. 1231 of 2021 on the file of the learned Judicial Magistrate, Melur, as the petitioner/A1 is concerned. For petitioner : Mr.M.Rajaraman ORDER https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P.(MD)No.23104 of 2022 2.When",
    "facts": "This petition has been filed to quash the proceedings in S.T.C.No. 1231 of 2021 on the file of the learned Judicial Magistrate, Melur. the matter is taken up for hearing, the learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that during the pendency of this petition, the petitioner /accused namely, G.Vijayakumar died and as such, there is no purpose in proceeding with the petition.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
